course: dictionary
lesson: 12913
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues around them tell you which one the writer means. The noun «establishment» is a good example. «This establishment does not allow dogs.» Here the sign is talking about a place, such as a shop, café or school.
explain: «The founders celebrated the establishment of their new school.» Now establishment means the act of setting something up or starting it. The clues are celebrated and new school: people celebrate when something new begins.
explain: «The Establishment wanted things to stay the same.» With a capital E, the Establishment means the group of powerful people who control a country or society. The clue is that they want things to stay the same, which powerful groups often do. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: An establishment is a business, organisation or place, such as a shop, restaurant, school or hotel.
fact: Establishment can also mean the act of setting something up or starting it.
fact: The Establishment, with a capital E, is the group of powerful people who control a country or society.
fact: Useful phrases: «the establishment of», «an educational establishment», «an eating establishment».
fact: The word comes from the verb «establish», which means to set up or start something.
exercise: «This establishment does not allow dogs.» In this sentence, what is an establishment? | A kind of dog | *A place, such as a shop or restaurant | A fast running race | A type of weather
exercise: «The founders celebrated the establishment of their new school.» What does establishment mean here? | *Setting something up or starting it | A place where you sleep | A long walk | A powerful group of rulers
exercise: «The Establishment wanted things to stay the same.» Which group does this mean? | A team of cooks | A set of tools | *The powerful people who control a country | A group of school children
test: «She ran an eating establishment by the harbour.» What kind of place is an eating establishment? | *A café or restaurant | A bus stop | A pond | A dentist's surgery
test: Which of these is an educational establishment? | A river | A bakery | *A school | A bus
exam: Which sentence uses establishment to mean a place? | Her cat sat on the mat. | The rain fell all day. | The children ran to the park. | *The shop is a well-known establishment on the high street.
